---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CheckboxDemo from '../../components/CheckboxDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Checkbox" description="A box for consent, permissions, filters, and row selection.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Checkbox</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A small box that is on, off, or mixed. Use it to confirm an action, grant a permission, pick items from a list, or
    select table rows.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <CheckboxDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Checkbox usage"
      code={`import { Checkbox } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/checkbox";
import { Label } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/label";

const [confirmed, setConfirmed] = useState(false);

<Label>
  <Checkbox checked={confirmed} onCheckedChange={setConfirmed} />
  I authorize this exact change
</Label>

<Checkbox id="share" defaultChecked />
<Label htmlFor="share">Share with selected workspace members</Label>

<Checkbox
  aria-label="Select all rows on this page"
  checked={all}
  indeterminate={some}
  onCheckedChange={selectAll}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass <code>checked</code> and <code>onCheckedChange</code> to control the box, or <code>defaultChecked</code> to
      let it keep its own state.
      <code>onCheckedChange</code> gets a boolean, so a state setter can be passed straight in.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <p>
      <code>variant</code> is <code>"default"</code> (fills with the primary color) or <code>"neutral"</code> (fills
      with the text color, for filter lists). There is one size: a 16px box with a 40 × 32px hit area.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>indeterminate</code> shows a minus sign and the mixed state, such as a "select all" box when only some rows
      are selected. Set
      <code>aria-invalid</code> to draw a danger border and ring while the box is unchecked. <code>disabled</code> dims
      the box and blocks changes; a disabled
      <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code> around it does the same.
    </p>
    <p>
      The box also takes Base UI props such as <code>id</code>,<code>name</code>, <code>value</code>,{' '}
      <code>required</code>,<code>readOnly</code>, <code>aria-describedby</code>,<code>inputRef</code>, and state
      functions for <code>className</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Checkbox renders an element with <code>role="checkbox"</code> and
      <code>aria-checked</code> (<code>"mixed"</code> when indeterminate), plus a hidden input for forms. Tab moves
      focus to it and Space toggles it. A focused box shows a 2px focus ring. Name every box with a wrapping
      <code>Label</code>, a <code>Label htmlFor</code>, an sr-only span, or
      <code>aria-label</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Color and check mark changes take 120ms and stop when reduced motion is requested. In forced colors mode the box
      gets a system border and a checked box is highlighted.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Off uses <code>--sprout-border</code> on <code>--sprout-surface</code>, and hover uses{' '}
      <code>--sprout-border-strong</code>. On uses
      <code>--sprout-primary</code> with <code>--sprout-on-primary</code>, so the opt-in TulipFarm theme tints it green.
      Neutral uses
      <code>--sprout-text</code> with <code>--sprout-surface</code>. Invalid uses <code>--sprout-danger</code>, and
      focus uses
      <code>--sprout-focus</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
